<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Niemodlin</h1><p class="st-meta">1313 CE – 1382 CE (approx.) · capital Niemodlin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Upper Silesian Piast duchy around the castle of Niemodlin, split from the Duchy of Opole in 1313 and reabsorbed in 1382.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On the death of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolko-i-of-opole">Bolko I of Opole</a> in 1313, his lands were divided among his sons. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-the-elder-of-niemodlin">Bolesław the Elder</a> received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niemodlin">Niemodlin</a> (Falkenberg), a castle town west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a>, as his own duchy. He was close to the Bohemian court and in 1327 did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-bohemia">King John of Bohemia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy consisted of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niemodlin">Niemodlin</a> and its surrounding villages, settled partly under German law, with the castle as the ducal residence. Its dukes depended on Bohemian patronage and on their cousins in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-opole">Duchy of Opole</a>. Little is recorded of its internal government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niemodlin">Niemodlin</a> line died out with Duke Henry in 1382, and the duchy returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-opole">Duchy of Opole</a>. Niemodlin later passed through various Silesian lords, went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1742 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-niemodlin.jpg" alt="Duchy of Niemodlin" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Duchy_of_Silesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1313 CE – 1382 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Niemodlin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bolesław the Elder</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Falkenberg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1348&amp;focus=duchy-of-niemodlin" aria-label="Duchy of Niemodlin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5067 406 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Niemodlin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5387 662L5408 675M5387 662L5330 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5408 675h0M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5387 662h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5387 662h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1348&amp;focus=duchy-of-niemodlin">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
